// Analyzed file list for nvdla_conv_pipeline.  Paths are relative to the
// PACKAGE ROOT: the elaboration recipe is sourced with the package root as cwd
// and `slang` runs from there too, so one spelling serves both.
//
// The round appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker to the end
// of this file (v5/round.py), which resolves to <run_root>/submission from the
// same cwd.  Keep the trailing newline and do not put a library directive
// after the file list -- an appended source line has to stay a source line.
//
// One `analyze -sv12` covers the whole list.  The generated NVDLA RTL is
// Verilog-2001 but declares no identifier that SystemVerilog-2012 reserves,
// which is what `nvdla_mcif_order` established for the same code generator.
+incdir+include

// `SYNTHESIS` selects the synthesizable branch and drops the X-injection tasks
// in `simulate_x_tick.vh`.  `VLIB_BYPASS_POWER_CG` makes every
// NV_CLK_gate_power a wire-through instead of a latch-based gate, so no SLCG
// can stop a clock -- which is what makes the CMAC's four-cycle latency and
// CBUF's six-cycle read latency mean what they say.  `DESIGNWARE_NOEXIST`
// selects NVDLA's own behavioural NV_DW02_tree / NV_DW_minmax / NV_DW_lsd over
// the Synopsys DesignWare cells, which are not in this repository.
+define+SYNTHESIS
+define+VLIB_BYPASS_POWER_CG
+define+DESIGNWARE_NOEXIST

// --- library cells and RAM models -------------------------------------------
// rtl/vlibs/* is upstream `vmod/vlibs`.  nvdla_conv_ram_models.sv is this
// task's functional replacement for the nine generated SRAM wrappers; the
// upstream wrappers instantiate foundry macros whose only models are
// simulation-only.
rtl/nvdla_conv_ram_models.sv
rtl/vlibs/NV_BLKBOX_SINK.v
rtl/vlibs/NV_CLK_gate_power.v
rtl/vlibs/NV_DW02_tree.v
rtl/vlibs/NV_DW_minmax.v
rtl/vlibs/NV_DW_lsd.v


